# --- Mission 02: Silent Salvage ---
# Your force is all you get. The factory changes flags, not hands.
unit 0 5 8 16
unit 0 5 8 20
unit 0 11 6 18 wrench
# The Directorate depot compound. The plant is ADR-008 surgery: the camp
# turret drew 20 against a supply of 0, which the turret gate would silence
# for the whole mission - the compound's teeth must be powered to bite.
structure 1 2 36 18 prize
structure 1 5 32 14 camp
structure 1 1 40 22 camp
unit 1 2 34 22 camp
unit 1 6 38 16 camp
trigger elapsed 90 -> message the_wire_is_cut
trigger entered 0 32 18 10 -> message they_know
trigger entered 0 32 18 10 -> spawn 1 2 46 19 2
trigger entered 0 32 18 10 -> assault 1 32 18
trigger owned prize 0 -> message flags_change
trigger owned prize 0 -> win 0
# THE DEFEAT PATH. The prize is taken by ENGINEER and the wrench is the only
# one you get, so losing it makes 'owned prize 0' unreachable and the mission
# ran forever: unwinnable, unlosable, undeclared. This is not a design call
# about when a raid has failed - it is the mission's own objective logic,
# since with no engineer there is no capture and therefore no win.
# 'rules noshortgame' above is correct and stays: this force has no
# structures at all, so the elimination rule would declare it defeated at
# tick 0. That is exactly why the loss has to be stated here instead.
#
# ORDER MATTERS AND MUST NOT BE CHANGED. The engineer is CONSUMED by a
# successful capture, so on a WIN both conditions are true on the same tick.
# Triggers evaluate in file order and DeclareWinner latches the first call,
# so 'win 0' above must stay ABOVE this block or a victory would be reported
# as a defeat. The mission02 gate holds this: it captures the prize, which
# consumes the wrench, and asserts the winner is still 0.
trigger destroyed wrench -> message the_wrench_is_lost
trigger destroyed wrench -> win 1
